WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:04.481
Vanessa Carlysle stole Wade Wilson's heart
in the 2016 hit Deadpool…

00:00:04.481 --> 00:00:07.860
"What's a nice place like you doing in a girl
like this?"

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.880
...and the actress who played her, Morena
Baccarin, stole viewers' hearts along the

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.880
way.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.180
Baccarin's been appearing in hit properties
since 2001, so you might feel like you've

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:22.570
seen her before—especially if you're a sci-fi
fan—but it may be hard to figure out exactly

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:23.570
where.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:27.050
Here's why Vanessa from Deadpool looks so
familiar.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.010
Way Off Broadway

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.329
Baccarin's first leading role came in the
small film Way Off Broadway, in which she

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:36.359
played a young actress trying to make it in
New York City.

00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:40.750
Her character Rebecca was one of a group of
friends struggling to find a way to turn their

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:45.579
artistic ventures into a career while also
dealing with her own personal anguish.

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:50.089
Although the drama wasn't seen by many, it
earned mostly good reviews, with Baccarin's

00:00:50.089 --> 00:00:53.969
performance in particular being singled out
for praise.

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:54.969
Firefly

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:59.690
In what's probably still her most well-known
small screen role, Baccarin played Inara on

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:02.390
Joss Whedon's short-lived series Firefly.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.691
While many of the planned storylines surrounding
the character were cut short when the series

00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:12.530
was canceled after just 14 episodes, Inara
was a fan favorite for her poise, charisma,

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:13.900
and intelligence.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:19.140
Despite Firefly's short run, the series became
a cult hit and, years after being canceled,

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:25.090
it was brought back for a feature film, Serenity,
in which Baccarin reprised her role.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:26.090
The O.C.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:31.500
It might take a hardcore fan of The O.C. to
remember much about Matt Ramsey, Sandy Cohen's

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.170
partner during his tenure as the lead of the
Newport Group.

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:40.570
Matt had a brief love interest in Baccarin's
Maya Griffin, the daughter of Sandy's rival

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:41.650
Henry.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:45.570
Although Baccarin only showed up in three
episodes of the series, her appearance is

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:51.080
still notable—it's where she first met her
future Gotham co-star and fiancé Ben McKenzie,

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.520
who starred as Ryan Atwood on the series.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.020
It wasn't love at first sight for the two,
though; in fact, McKenzie has said he doesn't

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:02.630
remember seeing Baccarin on set and thought
he was meeting her for the first time when

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:04.870
they reunited on Gotham.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.310
Awkward.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:08.440
How I Met Your Mother

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.430
Baccarin only appeared on one episode of How
I Met Your Mother, but it was an important

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:13.430
one.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:17.720
Her character arrived during Marshall and
Lily's season two break-up, with Baccarin

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:23.170
starring as Chloe, the only woman Marshall
actually dates during the brief separation.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:26.036
While Chloe didn't get a happy ending, she'll
always be remembered by How I Met Your Mother

00:02:26.036 --> 00:02:30.590
fans for inventing the name Swarley and pushing
the show's main couple back together.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.480
Stargate SG-1

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:37.360
With Firefly, Baccarin developed a following
in the sci-fi community—one she expanded

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.980
with her next few roles.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:43.220
Her first step back into genre fare came in
Stargate SG-1.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:48.300
The actress played the villainous Adria for
five episodes of the series and briefly reprised

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.420
the role in the movie Stargate: The Ark of
Truth.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:56.390
In addition to serving as her next big sci-fi
role, Stargate was also Baccarin's first real

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:01.340
chance to play a villain—a side she'd explore
in some of her later roles.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.440
V

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:08.459
Baccarin's next big role also involved playing
a sci-fi bad guy—this time in the ABC series

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:09.459
V.

00:03:09.459 --> 00:03:14.050
The revival of the high-concept '80s TV hit
featured Baccarin as Anna, the queen of an

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.270
invading alien species.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:21.910
Baccarin earned multiple Saturn Award nominations
and a Scream Award nomination for her work.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:26.810
Unfortunately, the series was plagued by low
ratings and high production costs, and was

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:30.050
canceled before it could reach a third season.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.770
Guest starring roles

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:36.560
Like many actors, Baccarin has made the guest
starring rounds on TV, appearing on shows

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:42.310
like Heartland, Numb3rs, Medium, and The Good
Wife, in addition to a multi-episode arc on

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.050
The Mentalist as a murderous matchmaker.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:49.630
Super fans of It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia
may also recognize Baccarin from the show's

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:53.690
unaired pilot, in which she played the transgendered
Carmen.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:57.349
Baccarin said she appeared in the episode
because she was college friends with writer

00:03:57.349 --> 00:04:02.460
and star Glenn Howerton, but she unfortunately
wasn't able to continue with the series due

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.260
to other commitments.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.410
Homeland

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:10.550
Baccarin earned an Emmy nomination for her
Homeland performance as Nick's wife, Jessica,

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:14.950
appearing consistently throughout the series'
first and second seasons, although she became

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.690
less of a staple in season three due to her
real-life pregnancy.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:23.440
Jessica was written off the show before the
fourth season, opening her up for other projects

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.930
where her character got a little better treatment.

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:31.150
Still, despite the fact that fans didn't enjoy
her character, Baccarin demonstrated her dramatic

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:35.430
chops and earned a major award nomination
to boot.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:36.660
Back in the Day

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:41.710
Making the jump to big screen comedies in
2014, Baccarin starred in Back in the Day,

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:45.630
created by and co-starring Smallville's Michael
Rosenbaum.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:50.300
The movie's tone didn't go over well with
critics, with the film amassing a terrible

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.240
11 percent on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:57.530
Fortunately, it didn't completely sink Baccarin's
comedy career.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.530
Spy

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:03.810
Baccarin's rebound came in the form of Spy,
a hit comedy that sits at a much more impressive

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:06.240
94 percent on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:11.470
In the movie, Baccarin plays Karen Walker,
the perfect super spy and a rival to Melissa

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:13.190
McCarthy's Susan.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:18.500
A solid comedy showcase for Baccarin, Spy
was also one of her most notable pre-Deadpool

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:24.330
big-screen roles, proving the TV star could
work in a big budget blockbuster.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:25.630
Gotham

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:30.580
Before Deadpool, Baccarin took on the role
of another beloved comic book character, portraying

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.229
Dr. Leslie Thompkins on Fox's Gotham.

00:05:33.229 --> 00:05:38.400
Her onscreen love story with Jim Gordon has
spilled over into real life, and she and Ben

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.449
McKenzie got engaged in 2016 shortly after
the birth of their daughter.

00:05:43.449 --> 00:05:47.930
Baccarin says Lee's pregnancy on Gotham wasn't
at all related to her own, though—just a

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:49.300
happy coincidence.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:52.770
Let's hope their real-life romance goes better
than it does on Gotham.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:54.400
Thanks for watching!

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.199
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:57.199 --> 00:05:59.580
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

